---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/base";
---

<Layout title="For Developers" description="Technical approach behind Tor Browser Installer.">
  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow"><Icon name="terminal" size={14} /> For Developers</span>
      <h1>Cross-platform Tor Browser installation, done right.</h1>
      
      <p class="lede" style="max-width: 68ch;">
        On Linux, <a href="https://flathub.org/apps/org.torproject.torbrowser-launcher">Tor Browser Launcher</a>
        does this as a Flatpak: fetch, verify, install, launch. It works, but it's Linux-only 
        and runs Python + GTK in a sandbox. This project does the same thing as a single 
        native Rust binary that compiles for macOS, Windows, and Linux.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid--3 dev-grid" style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <div class="card dev-card">
          <h3>One codebase, all platforms</h3>
          <p>
            Everything is in <code>install.rs</code>: fetch release JSON, download the bundle, 
            verify SHA-256, check PGP signature against the Tor Browser Developers key, 
            then install using platform-native methods. Platform differences use 
            <code>cfg(target_os = ...)</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card dev-card">
          <h3>No sandbox, no runtime</h3>
          <p>
            No Flatpak runtime or permission model. On macOS: mount DMG, copy app. 
            On Linux: extract tar.xz. On Windows: run NSIS installer silently. 
            Simple, direct, predictable.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card dev-card">
          <h3>Full transparency</h3>
          <p>
            Every command the app runs is logged to a visible panel in the UI as it 
            happens. Same principle as Tor Browser Launcher, now on every platform.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dev-note">
        <Icon name="info" size={18} />
        <div>
          <p>
            <strong>Note:</strong> This is an independent project, not a Tor Project product. 
            See the <a href={`${base}security`}>security page</a> for full verification details.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .dev-grid {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .dev-card {
    padding: 24px;
  }
  .dev-card h3 {
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .dev-card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .dev-note {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--app-purple-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--app-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
  }
  .dev-note :global(svg) {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .dev-note p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .dev-note a {
    color: var(--app-purple-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .dev-note a:hover {
    color: var(--app-purple-bright);
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .grid--3 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
